#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_indicator

#% text
# `discrete_indicator(x, x0, domain)` gives 1 if `x` equals `x0` and 0 if `x` is another element of the finite `domain`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the indicator of the single point `x0` on a finite domain of symbols or values.

#% item
# A `x0` outside the domain gives 0; an `x` that is not an element of the domain leaves the call unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_indicator(a, a, [a, b, c])
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
discrete_indicator(b, a, [a, b, c])
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
discrete_indicator(x, a, [a, b, c])
#% output
#= discrete_indicator(x, a, [a, b, c])

#% cell
table(discrete_indicator(v, 2, [1, 2, 3]), v, [1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [0, 1, 0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `kronecker_delta`, `boole`
